RF.put("questb:b61",{"8701":{"id":8701,"t":"Band of Veiled Shadows","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ceremonial Ring, 2 Onyx Idols, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ceremonial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Onyx Idol Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Sandstalker 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nBand of Veiled Shadows\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8621":{"id":8621,"t":"Stormcaller's Footguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of dominance and other minor components and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormcaller's Footguards\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Class Shaman Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8621\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stormcaller's Footguards this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"1581":{"id":1581,"t":"Elixirs for the Bladeleafs","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Elixirs of Lion's Strength and 2 Elixirs of Minor Defense to Syral Bladeleaf in Dolanaar.\n6 Elixir of Minor Strength\n2 Elixir of Minor Defense","desc":"Our herb and alchemy shop is booming, but my husband spends so much time mixing potions that we never have time for each other.\nCan you help us?\nIf you can bring me a supply of pre-made elixirs, then I would be happy to trade with you. I have some rare herbs that you might find useful.","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Earthroot 6 Mageroyal\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Do you have the elixirs to trade?","done":"These are nicely mixed. You take great care in your trade, ‹name›, and that is important for an alchemist.\nHere are your herbs, freshly gathered. May you use them well.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":57.7,"n":"Syral Bladeleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alchemy"]},"6941":{"id":6941,"t":"Call of Air - Vipore's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Lieutenant's Medal Winterax Warrior , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl , Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer and 4 more","back":"The elite Frostwolf units that guard the lines must be dealt with, soldier! I'm tasking you with thinning out that herd of savages. Return to me with medals from their lieutenants and legionnaires. When I feel that enough of the riff-raff has been dealt with, I'll deploy the air strike.","done":"The flight will be ready soon. Continue your efforts!\nStart Wing Commander Vipore Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Vipore Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6941","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6781":{"id":6781,"t":"More Armor Scraps","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Armor Scraps Winterax Warrior 80 % , Winterax Mystic 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % and 4 more","back":"‹name›, we need more armor scraps to supply our troops!","done":"These are some good pieces, ‹name›. I can use them to fashion new equipment for our troops.\nIf my supply level gets high enough, then maybe our seasoned fighting units will enter the field!\nStart Murgot Deepforge Alterac Valley End Murgot Deepforge Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6781\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Armor Scraps\nBring 20 Armor Scraps to Murgot Deepforge in Dun Baldar.\nMurgot Deepforge Alterac Valley\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] More Armor Scraps this quest\nMurgot Deepforge Alterac Valley","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7181":{"id":7181,"t":"The Legend of Korrak","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"According to legend, the leader of the mighty Winterax trolls appears at will to wreak havoc on the denizens of Alterac Valley.\nShould Korrak make himself known, destroy him and return to Warmaster Laggrond.\nKorrak the Bloodrager slain","desc":"The invading Stormpike are not the only threat in the region, soldier. The war in the Valley is waged on two fronts. The cannibal Winterax trolls also vie for power.\nThey are lead by Korrak the Bloodrager - a cruel and cunning beast.\nA strike against Korrak could prove to be a crushing blow to the Winterax clan. Slay the beast and be rewarded!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBloodseeker Ice Barbed Spear Wand of Biting Cold\nYou will also receive:\nRune of Recall\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7261":{"id":7261,"t":"The Sovereign Imperative","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Alterac Valley in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Outside of the entrance tunnel, find and speak with Lieutenant Haggerdin.\nFor the glory of Bronzebeard!","desc":"We are fighting a brutal battle in the valleys of Alterac. The cannibalistic Winterax trolls attack us from one side and the savage Frostwolf Clan from the other. Both must be exterminated in the name of King Magni Bronzebeard! The taking, culling, and turning of that land is a sovereign and territorial imperative to the kingdom of Ironforge.\nAlas, soldiers do not grow on trees! Report to Lieutenant Haggerdin outside Alterac Valley to begin your tour of duty and honor amongst the Stormpike.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Let's get to work!\nDun Morogh Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.3,"y":31.2,"n":"Lieutenant Rotimer","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7101":{"id":7101,"t":"Towers and Bunkers","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Capture an enemy tower, then return to Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl in the Alterac Mountains.\nTower Captured","desc":"Towers and bunkers are important positions, and we must capture and hold them all! So to that end, I want you to attack a bunker that is controlled by the enemy.\nTo do that, enter one with an Alliance banner. You will see another banner inside. Pull out that banner, and a white Horde banner will appear in its place. Well done!\nAt that point your task for me will be complete, but if you hold the place long enough, and if the Alliance doesn't take it back, then it will be destroyed!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You haven't yet assaulted a bunker, ‹name›! Are you waiting for others to claim your glory?","done":"I heard of your mission's success! That pleases me...\nOur troops can now charge forward with impunity, and show the Alliance that Alterac Valley is no place for them!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":65.6,"y":55.1,"n":"Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6861":{"id":6861,"t":"Zinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\n30 Thorium Bar\n50 Mithril Bar\n75 Iron Bar\nSteamsaw Alterac Ram in Alterac Valley , Frostwolf Warrior , Stormpike Guardsman in Alterac Valley , Commander Karl Philips in Alterac Valley and 1 more","desc":"null","rew":"You will receive:\nZinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit\n+25 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I'm as anxious as you are to try out my portable shredder unit, ‹race›, but before I can make the kit, I'm going to need materials - lots of materials!\nTo be exact, I'm going to need a mountain of thorium, mithril, and iron. I will also need one steamsaw per unit. You'll have to get those at the lumber mill.\nWhen I was nosing around in here (before my capture) I noticed a pile of steamsaws at the Stormpike lumber camp.\nMaster Engineer Zinfizzlex wants you to bring him the following:\nStart Master Engineer Zinfizzlex End Master Engineer Zinfizzlex Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6861","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"701":{"id":701,"t":"Guile of the Raptor","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 12 Raptor Hearts from Highland Fleshstalkers for Tor'gan.\n12 Raptor Heart Highland Fleshstalker 33 %","desc":"With some additional objects, I will be able to create an item that will imbue Gor'mul with the guile of the raptor! With the power of the raptor flowing through him, Gor'mul will know our new power and rediscover the warrior that lies dormant!\nI will require raptor hearts to fashion the item and spell.","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"My preparations are made, all I require are the raptor hearts.","done":"Yes, these will work perfectly. I will transfer their power and the spirit of the raptors into this orb. This orb will imbue Gor'mul with the fiery strength and intelligence of the raptor.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6621":{"id":6621,"t":"King of the Foulweald","lv":26,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound. Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner. Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.\nMurgut's Totem Chief Murgut , Murgut's Totem Basket\nProvided: Karang's Banner","desc":"‹name›, another tribe of Furbolgs, the Foulweald, live southeast of Astranaar. They are not as many as the Thistlefur, but their ferocity poses a future threat. With a show of force, we can remove that threat.\nTake this banner, go to the Foulweald village and place it on their totem mound. They will try to destroy the banner, but hold your ground until their chief, Murgut, appears to save face for the tribe. Bring me the totem he carries.\nGather your allies, ‹name›. This is no task for a single ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBoorguard Tunic Cobalt Legguards\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650","back":"Did you defeat Chief Murgut, ‹name›? Did you retrieve his Foulweald Totem?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Issuing that challenge to the Foulwealds and defeating their leader sends them a strong message:\nThe Horde is not to be trifled with.\nI don't believe that tribe will be giving us much trouble for a long time.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.9,"y":34.5,"n":"Karang Amakkar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1021":{"id":1021,"t":"Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!","lv":32,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Anilia in Xavian.","desc":"Listen, I don't know who you are, but I need your help. My sisters went to take back the Branch of Cenarius from the satyr. They said they'd be back soon, but it's been two whole days!\n‹name›, you have to find them! They were looking for the ruins of a night elf temple in Xavian to the northwest. I don't know what to think. Look for Anilia, she was leading them on the search.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Judging by the gaping wound in her side, Anilia is on the verge of death.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":21.7,"y":53.3,"n":"Illiyana","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":78.3,"y":44.8,"n":"Anilia","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3421":{"id":3421,"t":"Return Trip","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"I will return you to Sanath's camp now.\nDo not mind his bad manners--he is rude to everyone save for the master. Perhaps he shall learn his lesson one day.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":26.5,"y":46.3,"n":"Nyrill","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"3821":{"id":3821,"t":"Dreadmaul Rock","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture forth to the Burning Steppes and find out what became of Sha'ni Proudtusk.","desc":"Sha'ni was sent to investigate reports of strange ritualistic activity coming from the Firegut ogres of the Burning Steppes over three weeks ago.\nGoretooth tells me that he hasn't heard from anyone in that platoon and that it's best that I move on and focus on the task at hand. Can you believe it? That's my wife!\nI can't leave my post, ‹name›, but I must know what became of Sha'ni. Travel to the Burning Steppes and search for her.","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"My poor Thal'trak.\nWe were planning on moving in with my mother and father in the Hinterlands after our tours were over. Now those plans are ruined!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.4,"y":48.1,"n":"Thal'trak Proudtusk","s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3981":{"id":3981,"t":"Commander Gor'shak","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Commander Gor'shak in Blackrock Depths.\nYou recall that the crudely drawn picture of the orc included bars drawn over the portrait. Perhaps you should search for a prison of some sort.","desc":"Poor Gargal... didn't even see it coming. WHAM! The arrow landed dead center on the top of his head. He was no genius before but now...\n<Galamav grimaces.>\nWhen we dislodged the arrow, we noticed a rolled up note attached to the shaft. On the note was a crudely drawn picture of an orc behind bars with the signature of Commander Gor'shak attached.\nIf he's still alive in the Depths, you'll have to find him.\nA trap you say? Well no kidding, numb hooves! That's why you're going!","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"We haven't got much time. Listen carefully, ‹race›. What I have to tell you is classified and for your ears only.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":6,"y":47.7,"n":"Galamav the Marksman","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4701":{"id":4701,"t":"Put Her Down","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy the source of the worg menace. As you left Helendis, he shouted a name: Halycon. It is what the orcs refer to in regards to the worg.\nHalycon slain","desc":"You have no doubt seen the worgs which the Blackrock orcs command.\nIt is curious - no matter how many we destroy, their numbers never dwindle. My scouts have reported that the worgs are bred, trained, and ultimately exported from Blackrock Spire: capital city of the Blackrock orcs. You must travel to Blackrock Spire and discover the source of this menace. Discover... and destroy.\nGood luck, ‹name›. May Cenarius protect you...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAstoria Robes Traphook Jerkin Jadescale Breastplate\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you discovered and dealt with the source of the worg menace?","done":"Do not dwell upon her suffering, ‹name›. The beast was corrupt - a product of dark magic. You have done the Alliance a great service and you shall be rewarded.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":85.8,"y":68.9,"n":"Helendis Riverhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2621":{"id":2621,"t":"The Disgraced One","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Dispatch Commander Ruag in Stonard.","desc":"Regret. It is all I have now. One bad decision resulting in several horrible outcomes. If only I had waited for those orders. Maybe they would have detailed the horrors that awaited us in those cursed lands! Maybe they were to redirect us to another detail? Ultimately, it was my fault. All of it was my fault.\nSo here I stand, awaiting orders. I must know. I must have those orders.\nDispatch Commander Ruag resides in Stonard. Find him and find out what became of the orders.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","done":"Thrall's Grasp... The story is still fresh in my mind.\n<Commander Ruag shakes his head>\nTerrible thing that happened to that regiment. The horde lost some of its best soldiers when that battalion was destroyed.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.8,"y":54.9,"n":"Dispatch Commander Ruag","e":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"3501":{"id":3501,"t":"Everything Counts In Large Amounts","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kum'isha Imperfect Draenethyst Fragments and be rewarded for each one you turn in.\nImperfect Draenethyst Fragment Felcular 3 % , Ilifar 3 % , Kirith the Damned 3 % , Servant of Sevine 3 % and 4 more","desc":"Although you may never find a flawless sphere of draenethyst, you will undoubtedly uncover various imperfect fragments of the draenethyst in your exploration of these lands.\nWhile it is doubtful that Kum'isha will be able to use the flawed fragments to return home, the pieces may serve other, useful purposes for the draenei.\nReturn any piece of flawed draenethyst fragments that you may find and I shall reward you.","rew":"You will receive:\nKum'isha's Junk\nExperience: 5,650","back":"Have you had any luck in your exploration?","done":"You truly disgust me, ‹race›. A grown man drooling over a pile of junk? Pitiful! Take your reward and get out of my sight.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":52,"y":35.6,"n":"Kum'isha the Collector","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2701":{"id":2701,"t":"Heroes of Old","lv":57,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Open the chest and claim your reward.","desc":"Please, take from this a relic of old. We no longer have a use for the item.\nMay it serve you well in your fight against the legion.","rew":"You will receive:\nShard of the Splithooves\nExperience: 6,000","done":"You are temporarily blinded by the sparkle and gleam.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":33.3,"y":66.2,"n":"Spectral Lockbox","e":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4061":{"id":4061,"t":"The Rise of the Machines","lv":54,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Burning Steppes and recover 10 Fractured Elemental Shards for Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania.\nYou recall Theodora mentioning the golems and elementals of that region as being a source for these shards.\n10 Fractured Elemental Shard Greater Obsidian Elemental 50 % , War Reaver 50 % , Malfunctioning Reaver 50 %","desc":"The machines made themselves known to us during our initial forays into the Searing Gorge. Upon further investigation we discovered that they were being imported from Burning Steppes, possibly Blackrock Depths. That is what we need you for, ‹name›.\nYour first task is to venture to the Burning Steppes and recover elemental shards from the rock automatons and lesser rock creations of the region. Once you have collected a sufficient amount, return to me and I shall determine their source of origin.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do not take this task lightly, ‹name›!","done":"<Theodora lays the fragments out before her.>\n<Theodora carefully examines the fragments with an enormous monocle.>\nInteresting. Etched into the structural foundation of each of these fragments are... initials.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3,"y":47.8,"n":"Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97901":{"id":97901,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Jhag in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","done":"There you have it, you can craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folks don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to try it out.\nNo camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those as the basis of your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. Check in with someone who can train you in cooking if you haven't already learned the basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.6,"y":38.2,"n":"Jhag","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94301":{"id":94301,"t":"Craftsmans writ big voodoo robe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Big Voodoo Robe\nBig Voodoo Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Big Voodoo Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Big Voodoo Robe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94301","cats":["crafting"]},"94221":{"id":94221,"t":"Craftsmans writ golden rod","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Golden Rod\nGolden Rod","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Golden Rod, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"<The dwarf seems to be in a deep state of meditation, though your approach interrupted his focus. Fortunately, a smile greets you.>","done":"Ah, the Golden Rod I requested. I never expected it to arrive. I was considering going back to Ironforge to purchase one off the auction house. You saved me a trip, something these old feet greatly thank you for.\nI do not yet know how I can use this to commune with the Binding Stones, let alone if I even can, but I suspect this brings me one step closer.\nIn the worst case, well, I am happy to have a new cane.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":48.6,"y":55.7,"n":"Muggol Breezebeard","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7981":{"id":7981,"t":"1200 Tickets - Amulet of the Darkmoon","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nAmulet of the Darkmoon","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (1200)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7901":{"id":7901,"t":"Soft Bushy Tails","lv":60,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. No longer rewards Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket.","obj":"5 Soft Bushy Tail Maraudine Bonepaw 53.9 % , Magram Bonepaw 30.9 % , Mage Hunter 30 % , Feral Crag Coyote 29.9 % and 4 more","back":"It's amazing what people value! Take, for instance, a wooden stick with a soft bushy tail attached to it. Now, you and I might think something like that isn't all that valuable... but if you give that piece of junk a neat name like \"Savage Fuzz Tail\" and put it in a pretty box, then people will think it's valuable. Trash becomes treasure!\nGet me soft bushy tails from the wolves of Desolace and the Badlands, and I'll give you Darkmoon Faire tickets.","done":"Well done, ‹name›! These tails will make great prizes for our visitors, and that means happy visitors... who talk to their friends and bring more visitors!\nHere are your tickets! Have a good time at the Darkmoon Faire... and don't forget to tell your friends about us!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"5421":{"id":5421,"t":"Fish in a Bucket","lv":25,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 25 instead of 1. Pays 55s instead of 0.","obj":"5 Shellfish Shellfish Trap 84.9 % , Drysnap Crawler 1.7 % , Drysnap Pincer 1.5 %","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodbelly Fish\nMoney: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper","back":"I'll reward anyone who makes my life a bit easier... I enjoy doing as little as possible, mon!\nBelow the docks here in Shadowprey Village, I've many shellfish traps. If you're kind enough to do my work and collect me my shellfish, then I'll reward you with something you want... get my drift mon? For every five shellfish you bring me I will give you a fine Bloodbelly fish!","done":"Sweet mon, nothing beats work being done, especially if it's someone else doing the work... eh?","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":22.5,"y":73.1,"n":"Jinar'Zillen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5741":{"id":5741,"t":"Sceptre of Light","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Sceptre of Light and then return it to Azore Aldamort at the tower in Ethel Rethor.\nSceptre of Light Burning Blade Seer","desc":"The Burning Blade in Thunder Axe Fortress to the east is rumored to have acquired the Sceptre of Light from the Naga. Legend tells that the sceptre is able to sink entire cities under the great seas. The Burning Blade must not be allowed to possess such power.\nTo that end, you must retrieve the sceptre yourself! It is held by a Burning Blade seer, who studies the sceptre from atop one of the Thunder Axe watchtowers.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Do you have the Sceptre of Light?","done":"The elusive Sceptre of Light! Your acquisition of it has removed a grave threat to the world. Well done, ‹class›, well done.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":38.9,"y":27.2,"n":"Azore Aldamort","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5821":{"id":5821,"t":"Bodyguard for Hire","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Bodyguard for Hire .","obj":"Escort the Gizelton Caravan past the Kolkar Centaur village. Talk with Smeed at Scrabblescrew's Camp for your reward.","desc":"Under normal circumstances, Rigger and I would lead our kodo past the Kolkar Centaur. Every now and then we hear the Centaur war drums, and when we hear those we stop. It's not good for business to be dead!\nI'll tell you what ‹class›, if you protect us past the Kolkar village we'll make it worth your while.\nIt's just a short distance, all you need to do is keep the caravan intact and you can pick up your reward from Smeed Scrabblescrew - he is down the road a bit. We do a little business together.","rew":"You will receive:\nTrader's Ring\nExperience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Why do I find myself waiting for that blasted caravan?\n<Smeed looks enlightened.>\nOh yeah, they pay the bills. Have you seen them?","done":"You know, it doesn't seem prosperous to be paying the likes of you to guard Gizelton Caravan. ‹class›, if I were a bit taller I could take on a second job and sit kodo-side-saddle with the biggest gun my hands could carry... and I'd show them blasted centaur who's their papa.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":60.4,"y":38.1,"n":"Cork Gizelton","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":60.9,"y":61.9,"n":"Smeed Scrabblescrew","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5581":{"id":5581,"t":"Portals of the Legion","lv":38,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Banish 6 Portals at Mannoroc Coven and return to Taiga Wisemane at Shadowprey Village.\nHand of Iruxos\nPortals Banished : 0/ 6\nProvided: Hand of Iruxos","desc":"Behold - the Hand of Iruxos. A gruesome sight indeed.\nYou must possess it if the demon portals at Mannoroc Coven are to be banished... which is what I now ask you to do. The Demon threat is increasing and we must close these portals to stem the tide of demons to this world. Good luck, ‹name›... and be wary of the portal guardians.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGripsteel Wristguards Braidfur Gloves\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you banished the demon portals at Mannoroc Coven?","done":"You are to be commended, ‹name›. Your effort has helped greatly in fighting the demon threat, and all of Azeroth is safer because of it.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":25.8,"y":68.2,"n":"Taiga Wisemane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5501":{"id":5501,"t":"Bone Collector","lv":39,"min":33,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Kodo Bones from the Kodo Graveyard to Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut.\n10 Kodo Bone Kodo Bones , Kodo Bones","desc":"We're sitting on a goldmine here, I tell you - a goldmine! Kodo bones will change the world forever... I have customers making furniture, music instruments, and even blasting powder out of them.\nThere's a caravan that comes by and picks up my kodo bones and then sells them at Shadowprey Village. If you can travel to the kodo graveyard south of here and bring me ten kodo bones, I'll give you something in return. Is it a deal?","rew":"You will receive:\nKodobone Necklace\nExperience: 2,250\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Do you have the bones? The caravan will be here any moment. I need just ten more kodo bones to reach a career high. A career high, I tell you!","done":"Ah, goodie! My bones!\nI can't wait till the chaps at home see my face on the front cover of Goblin'preneur. I'll be the richest goblin in the world... and my physical education teacher said I would never amount to anything.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":62.3,"y":39,"n":"Bibbly F'utzbuckle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"6141":{"id":6141,"t":"Brother Anton","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Brother Anton in Desolace.","desc":"My brother in arms, Brother Anton, heard rumors of an undead infestation in distant Kalimdor, in a land known as Desolace. Anton immediately booked passage to that place, to seek and destroy the undead menace!\nHe is looking for those with the bravery and resolve to aid him. If your heart is true, then speak with Anton. He is in Desolace, in the Alliance town of Nijel's Point.","rew":"Experience: 300","done":"I received word of aid arriving from the east. Are you the source of these rumors? Have you come here to help the Scarlet Brother in its crusade?\nIf so, then listen close...\nStormwind City Desolace","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":52.6,"y":43.2,"n":"Brother Crowley","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":66.5,"y":7.9,"n":"Brother Anton","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7501":{"id":7501,"t":"The Light and How To Swing It","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nThe Light and How to Swing It A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: The Light and How to Swing It","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: The Light and How to Swing It End Lorekeeper Mykos Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Paladin Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7501","cats":["dire-maul"]},"221":{"id":221,"t":"Worgen in the Woods","lv":29,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Nightbane Dark Runner worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\nNightbane Dark Runner slain : 0/ 12","desc":"You might have noticed some larger worgen wandering around with the Shadow Weavers in the woods? From what we can tell, these Dark Runners make up the bulk of the worgen numbers.\nOn my rangings, I've also noticed that they have overrun the Rotting Orchard southwest of town. These worgen are a bit tougher than the last you faced.\nBe on your guard.","rew":"Money: 19 0 gold, 19 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Back so soon, ‹name›? I hope you haven't come to tell me you've given up.","done":"You performed well against the Dark Runners, ‹name›. But it seems as though their numbers are inexhaustible. Every time we make progress, more spring up to refill their ranks.\nWhat is the evil power that draws them here? Why have they come to disturb our unhappy realm...\nI will put my faith in Master Carevin. No doubt he will get to the bottom of the problem.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Calor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1261":{"id":1261,"t":"Marg Speaks","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Jeweled Pendant to Nazeer in Brackenwall Village.\nJeweled Pendant Muckshell Razorclaw 5 % , Muckshell Scrabbler 5 % , Muckshell Pincer 5 % , Muckshell Snapclaw 5 % and 2 more","desc":"Cursed muckshell! You can't kill Marg! Ah, but I am dead. So it must have slain me...\nBut my mission! My mission! You, ‹name›, must complete it.\nWhile near Theramore, I spied a group of Alliance soldiers camped on the beach. And one soldier wore a pendant... a pendant laden with more gems than any soldier could afford!\nThat night I snuck into their camp and stole the pendant, but on my return to base a muckshell crab-man killed me!\n‹name›, you must find that muckshell and recover the pendant!","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"‹name›, did you discover Marg's fate?","done":"This pendant was worn by a soldier of Stormwind??\nThank you, ‹name›. You have revealed the secret of Marg's death. But this pendant is a new mystery to solve, one that may have dire effects on the Alliance, and the Horde.\nStranglethorn Vale Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.6,"n":"Bubbling Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5181":{"id":5181,"t":"Villains of Darrowshire","lv":57,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skull of Horgus and the Shattered Sword of Marduk to Carlin Redpath at Light's Hope Chapel.\nSkull of Horgus Horgus' Skull\nShattered Sword of Marduk Shattered Sword of Marduk","desc":"The Annals of Darrowshire tells of the villains of that battle. It tells how the ghoul lord Horgus the Ravager was destroyed by Alliance forces during the battle. His body was cast into a lake, northwest of Corin's Crossing, and his skull remains there.\nMarduk the Black was never defeated, but his fabled sword was shattered and lost. It lies at the bottom of the gorge west of Corin's Crossing.\nRetrieve these items, ‹name›. I know not why, but I am certain their fate lies with you.","rew":"Experience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Did you find the skull and the sword, ‹name›?","done":"You found them! Well done, ‹name›! These relics hold a power I do not fully understand, a power you will one day harness.\nThey also bring dark memories to my mind, memories death and treachery, and of the last night of Darrowshire...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9181":{"id":9181,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Volcanic Hammer","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 3 Volcanic Hammers and the Craftsman's Writ - Volcanic Hammer - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Volcanic Hammer\n3 Volcanic Hammer\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Volcanic Hammer","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order BS-697:\n3 Volcanic Hammers.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These should go well with the dense weightstones we're stockpiling.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5261":{"id":5261,"t":"Eagan Peltskinner","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Eagan Peltskinner.","desc":"Eagan Peltskinner is looking for someone to hunt wolves for him. That's good news, because we're seeing a lot more wolves in Northshire Valley lately.\nIf you're interested then speak with Eagan. He's around the side of the abbey, to the left.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"That's true. I'm looking for someone to hunt me some wolves! Are you that person?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.2,"y":42.9,"n":"Deputy Willem","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":40.2,"n":"Eagan Peltskinner","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91741":{"id":91741,"t":"Nibbled on book","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return the book to Brother Paxton.\nProvided: Nibbled-On Book","desc":"<One of the kobolds dropped this book. It looks like the kobold might have tried to eat it.\nBrother Paxton inside the abbey has a small library he maintains. The book must have come from there.>","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 0 silver, 17 copper Experience: 85","back":"What's that you got there? It looks like one of my books.","done":"Hey! How did you end up with that? It's supposed to be on the shelf! Oh dear, the kobolds have been stealing my books again. They must want to eat them!\nThanks for bringing back the book, but what will I do about the rest of my missing collection?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"61":{"id":61,"t":"Shipment to Stormwind","lv":7,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring William's Shipment to Morgan Pestle in the Stormwind Trade District.\nWilliam's Shipment\nProvided: William's Shipment","desc":"My brother Morgan is waiting in Stormwind for my shipment of candles. I don't have enough time to make the trip myself, but if you'd like to take him the shipment, he'll pay you well.\nI've packed up the candles, and you can find Morgan in our shop, Pestle's Apothecary, in the Stormwind Trade District.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n15 Explosive Rocket 5 Oil of Olaf 2 Elixir of Minor Strength\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 800\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Oh, a shipment from my brother? Splendid! Fortune truly shines on me today!","done":"Here is your payment ... and while you're here, take a look around! I'm sure we have a potion or other trinket you'd find useful.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"William Pestle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Morgan Pestle","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4461":{"id":4461,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.1,"y":60.2,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4221":{"id":4221,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":39,"y":59.1,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8461":{"id":8461,"t":"Deadwood of the North","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Nafien would like you to kill 6 Deadwood Den Watchers, 6 Deadwood Avengers, and 6 Deadwood Shamans. Return to him in northern Felwood near the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.\nDeadwood Den Watcher slain : 0/ 6\nDeadwood Avenger slain : 0/ 6\nDeadwood Shaman slain : 0/ 6","desc":"There is a camp of Deadwood furbolgs directly to our southwest. Corruption permeates the camp, and I wish to put an end to it before they become a problem.\nThe Deadwood tribe is evil, but it is the effects of the fel that pollutes their minds. Their hostility is not truly an innate quality, yet they cannot be helped. It saddens me that we must fight our own brethren.\nPlease, ‹name› - I ask you to do what must be done. Simply spare me the details; such troublesome images upset me far too much.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLeggings of the Ursa Helm of the Pathfinder\nExperience: 5,650\n+150 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"Once you gain the trust of the Timbermaw, I am confident there will be something we will be able to do for you. The Timbermaw do not forget their allies, especially in dark times such as these.","done":"I sense that you have achieved victory. Victory... such a hollow word considering what had to be done. Regardless, you've proven yourself to be worthy of our trust.\nIt may take some time before the Timbermaw welcome you without hostility within the Hold. Still, your perseverance will erode any suspicion my brethren may have about you. So long as you never betray us and raise weapons against us, we will find common ground.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":64.8,"y":8.1,"n":"Nafien","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2941":{"id":2941,"t":"The Borrower","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the letter to Curgle Cranklehop in Tanaris.\nA Short Note\nProvided: A Short Note","desc":"I have studied many subjects in my time, and my latest fascination is with the snapjaw that occupy the beach in the Hinterlands. There's one in particular I'd like to see, a giant snapjaw named Gammerita. I'd like to go myself, but my research keeps me here. I think a picture of her would be the next best thing.\nTake this letter to Curgle Cranklehop in Tanaris. She has created an invention for me that can capture a picture. She called it a \"snapshot\", I think...","rew":"Experience: 1,100","back":"A letter -- for me?","done":"Are you another one of Daryn's interns? She's quite a knowledgeable historian, ‹name›. You should be grateful to be studying under her leadership.\nNow, let me get the Super Snapper FX. You're gonna love it!\nTeldrassil Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"8221":{"id":8221,"t":"Rare Fish - Keefer's Angelfish","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0. Pays 23s instead of 0.","obj":"Keefer's Angelfish","rew":"You will receive:\nLucky Fishing Hat\nMoney: 23 0 gold, 23 silver, 0 copper","back":"*Whir* *Click*\nI seek rare fish for Fishmaster Bluegill to catalogue. If you bring me a Keefer's Angelfish, I will provide you with this fine reward.\n*Zzzap* *Whir*","done":"*Whir*\nIdentification of Keefer's Angelfish complete.\nYour Reward is now available.\n*click-click* *Bzzzz*","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":76.9,"n":"Fishbot 5000","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"541":{"id":541,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":30,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Dun Garok and kill 8 Mountaineers, 4 Riflemen, 2 Priests and Captain Ironhill and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nDun Garok Mountaineer slain : 0/ 8\nDun Garok Rifleman slain : 0/ 4\nDun Garok Priest slain : 0/ 2\nCaptain Ironhill slain","desc":"Dwarves aiding the humans? Damn those filthy little beasts.\nWe shall test the strength of the so-called Alliance. We'll see how anxious those little ankle-bashers are to help the humans once they feel our wrath. We know exactly where their stronghold is in this territory.\nThey have established a barracks in southeastern Hillsbrad along Thoradin's Wall called Dun Garok. The final mission of this battle is to lay siege on Dun Garok, ‹class›. Captain Ironhill, their leader, must die.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Dun Garok proves to be too much of an obstacle for you, ‹class›? And here I thought you had established yourself valiantly in Hillsbrad.\nIf you're not up to handle the mission assigned to you, I will find another who can produce better results. As for you, well, I am sure the Dark Lady could always use more grave diggers back in Tirisfal Glades.","done":"Your actions on the battlefield are worthy of the highest praise.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6061":{"id":6061,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame an Adult Plainstrider. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"As a tauren, it is important to follow the traditions of our ancestors by fighting mighty creatures. By besting these creatures, we are able to intake their spirits, allowing us to become closer to the Earthmother.\nIn the same way, taming a beast to fight alongside us helps us become one with nature around us. Eventually, you will learn to tame a beast of your choosing. But all things take practice, and you have much to learn. Begin by taking this taming rod; you must tame an adult plainstrider.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Practice your skills, ‹name›. Tame the adult plainstrider.","done":"Signs have appeared to me from the Earthmother; you have done well.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9261":{"id":9261,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of Ironforge","lv":10,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Ironforge and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Ironforge from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nDun Morogh Elwynn Forest Tirisfal Glades Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":53,"y":35,"n":"Lieutenant Nevell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"9341":{"id":9341,"t":"Tabard of the Argent Dawn","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"10 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nTabard of the Argent Dawn","back":"You have aided our cause greatly, ‹name›. If you wish, I can make available the tabard of the Argent Dawn. We are proud to have you among our allies.","done":"Take this tabard and wear it proudly. Perhaps your deeds might inspire others to take up arms in support of our fight against the Scourge.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":72.6,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":45.4,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"301":{"id":301,"t":"Report to Ironforge","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Ironband's Progress Report to Prospector Stormpike.\nIronband's Progress Report\nProvided: Ironband's Progress Report","desc":"We'll need approval to get Ironband more blastpowder. You'll have to take his report to the Explorers' League headquarters in Ironforge.\nHere's the report. Give it to Prospector Stormpike, and don't forget to duck after you deliver it. Stormpike is hotheaded, and he won't be happy to hear of Ironband's slow progress at the site.\nYou'll find Stormpike in the Assembly of Explorers.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"We Stormpikes don't like being bothered with trivial matters, ‹class›. I hope you brought news worthy of my valuable attention.","done":"Curse that Ironband! I sent him a load of blastpowder weeks ago, but he's made no mention of it in this report.\nSo...where did the blastpowder go?!?\nLoch Modan Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Jern Hornhelm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"781":{"id":781,"t":"Attack on Camp Narache","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bristleback Attack Plans to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache.\nBristleback Attack Plans\nProvided: Bristleback Attack Plans","desc":"After carefully evaluating the map, you realize that what you discovered are the plans made by the Bristleback warchief for an extended siege on Camp Narache.\nSurely Chief Hawkwind could use this information!","rew":"You will receive:\nThick Bark Buckler\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You have a look of concern about you, ‹name›. What news do you bring?","done":"This is quite alarming indeed! But with this information we can call on our brethren from Bloodhoof Village to help thwart the attack. You have saved the lives of many tauren, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":59.8,"y":82.2,"n":"Dirt-stained Map","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"99101":{"id":99101,"t":"Our ancient enemy","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Longwalker Malah's Report to Baine Bloodhoof.\nProvided: Longwalker Malah's Report","desc":"Baine Bloodhoof leads our village. He must know of this incursion at once.\nBring him Longwalker Malah's report. You will find him at the center of town.\nQuickly, now. There is no time to waste!","back":"What is it you bring me, ‹class›?","done":"<Baine reads the report, his gaze darkening.>\nThis will not stand. Thank you for delivering it to me, Vanyel.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.6,"y":63,"n":"Brave Wildrunner","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.4,"y":60.2,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"861":{"id":861,"t":"The Hunter's Way","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Flatland Prowler Claws to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\n4 Flatland Prowler Claw Flatland Prowler 41 %","desc":"You are eager to explore, I can tell. I too had the lust to wander, once...\nWander, and hunt. For hunting is a Tauren's greatest honor.\nIf you truly wish to follow the ways of the hunter, then Melor Stonehoof can show you the path. He is in Thunder Bluff, on the Hunter's Rise.\nAnd to show him your skill and resolve, bring him the claws of the flatland prowlers of Mulgore. They are tough and cunning -- fitting prey for a young ‹class› on the hunter's path.","rew":"Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Greetings. There is an air about you that tells me much. Do we have business, you and I?","done":"Skorn Whitecloud is a wise tauren. He has hunted for years and years, and although his body is old, his spirit burns fiercely. We are honored to have him with us.\nIf Skorn sent you to me, then you too must have the hunter's spirit. And to have gathered these claws shows your burgeoning skills.\nPerhaps you are ready to walk the path.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46,"y":63.4,"n":"Skorn Whitecloud","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9101":{"id":9101,"t":"Frostfire Belt","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Frostfire Belt if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Belt, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Arcane Crystals and 2 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Belt Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Belt\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n,you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Belt.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7661":{"id":7661,"t":"Wolf Swapping - Red Wolf","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horn of the Red Wolf","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHorn of the Swift Brown Wolf Horn of the Swift Gray Wolf Horn of the Swift Timber Wolf","back":"If you bring me your old fast wolf, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new wolf will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift wolves we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":69.4,"y":12.2,"n":"Ogunaro Wolfrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7341":{"id":7341,"t":"A Fair Trade","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"200 Thorium Shells sold by Jimmy McWeaksauce","rew":"You will receive:\n200 Thorium Headed Arrow","back":"Greetings, ‹race›. I am Kolark, Bounty Hunter from Thunderbluff. Much of the world I have traveled and much I have seen.\nMy journeys across the South Seas led to the discovery of these wonderous thorium headed arrows. Alas, I have an endless supply of the arrows but have exhausted my supply of shells. Bah, no self respecting Tauren would ever be caught dead using a flimsy bow. The arrows are useless!\nI will offer a trade: An even exchange of thorium shells for my thorium headed arrows. Deal?","done":"Excellent! I am a Tauren of my word, ‹race›. The arrows are yours.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":74.6,"y":24.1,"n":"Bounty Hunter Kolark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9021":{"id":9021,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Dreadmist Sandals, Dreadmist Leggings and Dreadmist Mantle.\nDreadmist Sandals Baroness Anastari 0 % in Stratholme\nDreadmist Leggings Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nDreadmist Mantle Jandice Barov 17 % in Scholomance\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Sandals Deathmist Leggings Deathmist Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"4941":{"id":4941,"t":"Eitrigg's Wisdom","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Eitrigg in Orgrimmar. When you have discussed matters with Eitrigg, seek council from Thrall.\nYou recall having seen Eitrigg in Thrall's chamber.","desc":"Rend lives?\nImpossible!\nIt had been thought that Rend was slain decades ago.\nSeek out the wisdom of Eitrigg, ‹name›. None know the workings of the Blackrock better than he and if what is written here bares truth, Eitrigg should be informed. No person should be denied the right of vengeance.\nYou will find him in Orgrimmar.\nOnce you have spoken with Eitrigg, confer with the Warchief to find out what he wishes to do about this problem.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Can you not see that I must not be interrupted?","done":"<Thrall appears dismayed by the news you bring.>\nBadlands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.8,"y":47.5,"n":"Warlord Goretooth","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8941":{"id":8941,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Shadowcraft Belt and a set of Shadowcraft Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nShadowcraft Belt Blackhand Assassin 7 % , Smolderthorn Shadow Hunter 3.1 % , Bloodaxe Warmonger 2.1 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 2.1 % and 3 more\nShadowcraft Gloves Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin 0 %","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Gloves Darkmantle Belt\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"3101":{"id":3101,"t":"Consecrated Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Consecrated Letter and speak to Brother Sammuel in Northshire Abbey.\nConsecrated Letter\nProvided: Consecrated Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Brother Sammuel, our local paladin trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Finally! We meet face to face, brother to brother. I welcome you to Northshire. This will be your home for a short time while you learn the ins and outs of how things are done, but know that Stormwind is not far off, and sooner or later, your path will take you there. But until then, be patient... Knight of the Silver Hand.","done":"In the meantime, you should know one or two other things. You are a symbol to many here in this land--act accordingly. The Holy Light shines within you, and it will be obvious to both your allies and your enemies.\nAlso, as you gain in wisdom and power, you will need to train to learn new abilities. That's where I come in. When you feel you've gained some experience here in Northshire, come back to me and I will teach you what I feel you are ready to learn. Good luck... ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.4,"y":42.1,"n":"Brother Sammuel","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1661":{"id":1661,"t":"The Tome of Nobility","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"I greet you once again, ‹name›. I am more proud to call you brother/sister than ever before--your dedication is a tribute to us all.\nThe time has come for me to bestow a great gift upon you. But know this, for now I give you this freely, but later, when time permits, this will be a much greater challenge to all paladins who choose to undertake my quest.\nSpeak to me again and I shall grant you a great boon.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Warhorse","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5661":{"id":5661,"t":"Touch of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"You be far from home out here in the Bloodhoof Village, ‹name›. I be sent here to find priests of my own tribe to send back to speak to our leaders, but that not mean I cannot help you too.\nI hear word that your head priestess spirit want all Forsaken to come to her--there are things you must learn.\nGo to meet Aelthalyste in the War Quarter in that city of yours.","rew":"You will learn: Touch of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"Ah, good, another has arrived. Time may not matter to me, but to you it is of the essence. There is much for you to learn and there is much I wish to teach you. You simply must prove your worth. Do that, and you shall be greatly rewarded.\nThunder Bluff Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.3,"y":15.3,"n":"Miles Welsh","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"3341":{"id":3341,"t":"Bring the End","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Andrew Brownell wants you to kill Amnennar the Coldbringer and return his skull.\nSkull of the Coldbringer Amnennar the Coldbringer in Razorfen Downs","desc":"In the Barrens lies a horrid mess of tangled vines called Razorfen Downs. While our first observations of this place revealed little threat, our recent findings are much more serious...\nThe quilboar of Razorfen Downs have aligned themselves with the Scourge. A Lich named Amnennar the Coldbringer rules them now, using the power of his massive consciousness to control their every move.\nAmnennar has a direct telepathic link to Ner'zhul; we must sever this bond, ‹name›. An end must come to the Coldbringer.","rew":"You will receive:\nVanquisher's Sword Amberglow Talisman\nExperience: 4,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"This matter is of utmost importance, ‹name›. We must stop any attempt by the Scourge to bolster their ranks.","done":"The loyalty of a Lich is unswerving, ‹name›. Let them know that such loyalty will only bring them destruction.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":74,"y":33.3,"n":"Andrew Brownell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"1101":{"id":1101,"t":"The Crone of the Kraul","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Quilboar Blaster.","obj":"Bring Razorflank's Medallion to Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar.\nRazorflank's Medallion Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul","desc":"Poor Heralath! And this dwarf... Lonebrow. What a brave soul he was.\nWe must not let their valiance go for naught. This crone... Charlga Razorflank ... must be stopped.\nSurely, infiltrating the Kraul will be perilous. There isn't time to send word to Darnassus. ‹name›, assemble a party to slay the crone.\nBring me Razorflank's Medallion as proof of demise.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBerylline Pads Stonefist Girdle Marbled Buckler\nNew in Forever: Quilboar Blaster.\nYou will also receive:\nQuilboar Blaster\nExperience: 3,350","back":"So long as Charlga Razorflank is mustering a force in Razorfen Kraul, these lands are in great danger.","done":"The crone has been laid to rest. This is fantastic news, ‹name›.\nIn these times of peril, it is refreshing to see one as brave as yourself.\nWith Razorflank's minions taken care of, our studies in the area can continue. Perhaps now we can gain further knowledge of exactly what happened to corrupt the resting place of Agamaggan.\nHowever, I fear the answer to that question lies in treachery as well...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":89.6,"y":46.6,"n":"Falfindel Waywarder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"3741":{"id":3741,"t":"Hilary's Necklace","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Hilary's Necklace, and return it to Hilary in Lakeshire.\nHilary's Necklace Glinting Mud","desc":"My friend Hilary lost her necklace, and we can't find it. We've been fishing all day right here, and we looked around here already. The only thing I can think of is that it fell into the lake. Our parents don't want us to swim in the lake... my mom says there's some mean things underwater, but you look like you aren't scared of mean things.\nCould you find it for her, please?","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hi. I miss my necklace. My daddy got it for me. Daddy says that there are monsters in the lake. Did you beat up any monsters?","done":"Thank you for finding my necklace mister ‹class›... you are very kind! My kitty thanks you too - isn't that right Effsee?","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.2,"y":53.6,"n":"Shawn","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.2,"y":53.6,"n":"Hilary","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"2381":{"id":2381,"t":"Plundering the Plunderers","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Southsea Treasure back to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet. Do not forget to get an E.C.A.C. and Thieves' Tools from Wrenix's Gizmotronic Apparatus. You will need both of these items to complete your mission.\nShould you be attacked by any unusually hostile parrots, use your E.C.A.C.!\nSouthsea Treasure Polly","desc":"I don't mean to scare you, ‹name›, but the last five thieves I sent to steal the southsea treasure came back to me in pieces.\nSouth along the coast you'll find Tide Razor, the southsea freebooter's ship. Nestled in the hold is the payoff - the southsea treasure. On the second level of that ship is the pirate's den, a place where they train all of their thieves.\nBoard that ship, steal the treasure, and bring it back to me. Use the pirate's den if you need to practice your thievery, but be careful!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Thistle Tea\nExperience: 1,350","back":"Well, at least you still have all of your body parts. Did you find the treasure?","done":"Incredible! Improbable! Simply amazing! You've got talent, Weir. Either that or you're the luckiest man alive!\nHere's your cut of the action. I'm sure you would make better use of this stuff than I could.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.1,"y":36.3,"n":"Wrenix the Wretched","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"96781":{"id":96781,"t":"Whats the big idea","lv":36,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Steal Barton's Scouting Report by pickpocketing it from him. Then, bring the report to Myrokos Silentform at Ravenholdt Manor.\nBarton's Scouting Report","desc":"We have noticed a Syndicate scouting party prowling around the ruins of Alterac, led by a man named Barton.\nThey're clearly searching for something, but I cannot know what without reading his scouting reports.\nI ask that you pickpocket the report from him, rather than killing him outright. Barton's death will tip off the Syndicate that we're on to them, and they will certainly take counter-measures to cover their tracks.\nIf you hope to find him, he is most likely among the Syndicate at Strahnbrad.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":85,"y":80.4,"n":"Myrokos Silentform","s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"6701":{"id":6701,"t":"Syndicate Emblems","lv":60,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Syndicate Emblem","back":"We have been entrenched in a battle with the Syndicate for years. What they lack in skill they make up for in numbers. It's impossible to kill them off fast enough to have any noticeable impact on their population!\nWe've found that the best way to deal with their size is to pilfer their emblems. Once an emblem is stolen the shamed member is 'dealt' with internally.\nPick their pockets clean and turn the emblems in to me or one of the other guards.\nStart at Durnholde, south of here.","done":"Hey, nice work! Keep this up and the other rogues might stop spitting on you.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":81.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Ravenholdt Guard","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":77.2,"y":20.1,"n":"Ravenholdt Guard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"5341":{"id":5341,"t":"Barov Family Fortune","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Alexi Barov when you have completed this task.\nThe Deed to Brill The Deed to Brill in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Caer Darrow The Deed to Caer Darrow in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Southshore The Deed to Southshore in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Tarren Mill The Deed to Tarren Mill in Scholomance","desc":"Within the Scholomance lays the Barov family fortune. I, Alexi Barov, am one of the last two remaining heirs of the house Barov. My brother, Weldon, is the other.\nWeldon, the miserable coward, fled during the war and thus retained his worthless existence as a human.\nHe now searches for the deeds so that he may claim the fortune for his own. Recover the deeds before my brother does and I shall make you wealthy beyond your wildest dreams!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"Bow your head in my presence, ‹race›. I am a noble, after all, and you are a copperless peasant.","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Now to secure my inheritance...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":71.6,"n":"Alexi Barov","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"3181":{"id":3181,"t":"The Horn of the Beast","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,450 experience instead of 5,417, 1.01 times as much.","obj":"Take Margol's Gigantic Horn to Mountaineer Pebblebitty.\nMargol's Gigantic Horn\nProvided: Margol's Gigantic Horn","desc":"The gigantic horn has numerous scratches and cracks. An unusual metal object is lodged into the rough surface.\nUpon further examination, you notice that the metal is actually a broken axe head. On the metal, the following words are etched:\nProperty of Mountaineer Pebblebitty.\nWhen you try and dislodge the broken axe head, it shatters into a million pieces.\nWoops!","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"No, I will not open the gate.","done":"What have you got there? A fake obviously!\nI've been face to face with Margol and I know for a fact that her horn is at least eight times larger than the one you've got in your hands, ‹name›. You probably got that off of a stormsnout in the Barrens. No ma'am, you can't fool Pebblebitty!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":18.2,"y":84,"n":"Mountaineer Pebblebitty","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"7021":{"id":7021,"t":"Great-father Winter is Here!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend! Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter, who's currently in Orgrimmar! If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil. Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!\nAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year. We have a great selection to choose from. Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.\nIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8861":{"id":8861,"t":"New Year Celebrations!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 70. Requires level 1 instead of 60. Pays 9s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Smokywood Supplies to Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff.\nSmokywood Supplies\nProvided: Smokywood Supplies","desc":"Thunder Bluff is holding a celebration for the new year! All day you'll find free booze there, and at night they'll put on a firework show!\nIt should be pretty nice... but Booty Bay is also having a party today; I bet it'll be even better!\nWell anyway, Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff needs a supply of Smoky Wood Pasture fare to help feed all the party goers. Can you do me a favor and deliver it!\nThanks, ‹name›! Innkeeper Pala is in the inn near the bridge to Hunter's Rise.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Good day, ‹class›! Did you come to Thunder Bluff for our celebrations? Or are you here to rest a weary hoof between hunts?","done":"Oh, very good! These supplies will help feed all our people, here to celebrate the new year!\nI thank you, ‹name›. You are in my debt. Please, take these coins... and heed my advice - drink heartily from the kegs outside, and join our revelers in a dance of celebration!\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Stranglethorn Vale Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.9,"y":71.4,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":53.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.5,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":64.7,"n":"Innkeeper Pala","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8381":{"id":8381,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Pants Sandworm Skin Gloves\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8781":{"id":8781,"t":"Arms for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Moonsteel Broadswords to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade Outpost outside of Hive'Zora. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\n2 Moonsteel Broadsword\nLogistics Task Briefing VI\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VI","desc":"The Ironforge Brigade has been a worthy ally in our fight in Silithus. Unfortunately, many of their supplies were lost on their way here. Procure a batch of weapons and deliver them to Janela Stouthammer near Hive'Zora.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","done":"Oh, excellent! I won't have to hear complaints about dull blades anymore. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":32.9,"y":52.5,"n":"Janela Stouthammer","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8541":{"id":8541,"t":"Grinding Stones for the Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Dense Grinding Stones, 10 Solid Grinding Stones and 10 Heavy Grinding Stones to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing III in order to complete this quest.\n10 Dense Grinding Stone\n10 Solid Grinding Stone\n10 Heavy Grinding Stone\nLogistics Task Briefing III\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing III","desc":"The Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of grinding stones. Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":33.7,"n":"Vish Kozus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8301":{"id":8301,"t":"The Path of the Righteous","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 200 Silithid Carapace Fragments and return to Baristolth.\n200 Silithid Carapace Fragment Supreme Silithid Flayer , Hive'Regal Hive Lord , Hive'Regal Slavemaker , Hive'Regal Spitfire and 4 more\nProvided: Agent of Nozdormu","desc":"The Brood of Nozdormu are naturally distrusting of the lesser races. While it is true that you have proven to me that you have the potential makings of a hero, the time has come to prove this to my master.\nHive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, Hive'Regal: All swarming with activity and all a threat to our existence. Slay silithid at these hives and take from them a fragment of their carapace. When you can carry no more, return to me and I shall strengthen your resolve.","rew":"You will receive:\nProxy of Nozdormu\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"There is much history rooted in their distrust of the mortal races; but alas, such is a tale better left for the Brood to tell when the time is right.","done":"You are not alone, hero. I will now grant you the ability to deputize others to help you in your quest. If you are to be the champion of your people, you will need assistance in your tasks and duties.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":36.4,"n":"Baristolth of the Shifting Sands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"461":{"id":461,"t":"The Hidden Niche","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Alaric to the hidden alcove.\nAlaric's Remains\nProvided: Alaric's Remains","desc":"I know of a hidden niche within the keep that holds an item dear to Thule, and his old colleagues. It also holds something you might find useful. Take me there!\nThe alcove is in the southwestern tower of the keep, behind a dusty shelf.\nTake my body, but leave my boots. They never fit me anyway...","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"This is the spot! Bring me closer...","done":"There we are, it's open. Leave me here. I spent the best days of my life in this keep, and the thought of resting within its walls gives me comfort.\nBe sure to close the alcove tight - I don't want those Rot Hides to find me.\nOh, and take this. You've earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":67.9,"y":24.9,"n":"Shallow Grave","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65.4,"y":24.8,"n":"Dusty Shelf","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"95981":{"id":95981,"t":"Watching the roads","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Dalaran Wizards and 8 Dalaran Watchers for Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher.\nDalaran Watcher slain : 0/ 8\nDalaran Wizard slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.\nSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoadwatcher's Confidence\nMoney: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ever since the barrier went down around Dalaran, the Kirin Tor have maintained a death grip on the roads. They're paranoid about something, that much is certain.\nFor now, however, the why is irrelevant.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":41,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"6461":{"id":6461,"t":"Blood Feeders","lv":19,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Xen'zilla at Malaka'Jin needs you to kill 10 Deepmoss Creepers and 7 Deepmoss Venomspitters.\nDeepmoss Creeper slain : 0/ 10\nDeepmoss Venomspitter slain : 0/ 7","desc":"We Trolls here at Malaka'Jin have prospered from the land; Stonetalon Mountain offers great hunting for us to live on.\nLately, we have attracted the wrong dinner guests... the spiders in these mountains have been raiding our camps at night looking to steal our hunt.\nIf you were to help us kill off these ghastly beasts we at Malaka'Jin would be in your debt. Spiders are everywhere in Stonetalon - just head north from here and you will see what I am talking about.","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Hey mon, have you slain the hairy blood feeders? I fear none here in Stonetalon but I don't go walking around here at night... if you know what I mean mon!\nAs long as I stay off their dinner plate then all is well.\nGood luck to you, ‹class›!","done":"Sweet, mon! Good news, perhaps we will have fewer unwanted dinner guests tonight.\nMany thanks, ‹name›. We are forever in your debt.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":71.2,"y":95,"n":"Xen'Zilla","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6301":{"id":6301,"t":"Cycle of Rebirth","lv":23,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat wants you to gather 10 Gaea Seeds.\n10 Gaea Seed Gaea Seed","desc":"Industrial greed and continuous war have wrecked the lands of Stonetalon. Only the blessings of the Earthmother can cure such injury.\n‹name›, I will require you to seek a special seed, the Gaea seed. They are only found here in Stonetalon Mountain, north of Sun Rock Retreat at Mirkfallon Lake, near the water's edge.\nOnce you bring me the seeds I will imbue them with shamanistic power to speed their growth.","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,400\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The continuous destruction caused by war and those that seek a profit from lumber pains me deeply. The least I can do is perform the cycle of rebirth and sow the Gaea seeds to replenish the lands with a new forest. Do you have the required Gaea seeds, ‹class›?","done":"Ah? ‹name›, you have the Gaea seeds. Watch and you shall see the power that these seeds will do for the land. Only those pure and true can heal the land?\n<Tammra begins to chant.>","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Tammra Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6381":{"id":6381,"t":"New Life","lv":25,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Plant 10 Gaea Seeds in Gaea Dirt Mounds, and then return the remaining Enchanted Gaea Seeds to Tammra at Sun Rock Retreat.\nEnchanted Gaea Seeds\nGaea seed planted : 0/ 10\nProvided: Enchanted Gaea Seeds","desc":"As you have seen, ‹class›, though the land is in pain, the cycle of life is a powerful thing. Now we must do our part help it along. You must plant these seeds at the center of the destruction, to the west, in the Charred Vale. Beware, for harpies and angry fire elementals still plague the scarred land.\n‹name›, take these enchanted Gaea seeds and plant them in fertile mounds of soil. The cycle of life must go on!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWindseeker Boots Sandspire Gloves\nExperience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"These seeds you plant are strong, resisting corruption, and making a foothold for other life. They will grow and grow, first preventing corruption and healing the scarred land, and then one day, restoring Stonetalon to a lush forest, once again.\nHave you planted all of the Gaea seeds?","done":"This is great victory for the land. In time, other things will come to pass: the Venture Co. will pack up their buzz saws and axes, the angry fire spirits will calm, and the harpies will be pushed out by the land.\nOnly then ‹name›, will Stonetalon be truly at peace.\nYou have done well ‹class›; take one of these items as thanks for the new life you have created here today.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Tammra Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"621":{"id":621,"t":"Zanzil's Secret","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 samples of Zanzil's Mixture to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\n12 Zanzil's Mixture Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\" 33 % , Jon-Jon the Crow 33 % , Zanzil the Outcast 33 % , Zanzil Naga 33 % and 3 more","desc":"Zanzil the Outcast dwells with his followers in the Jubuwal and Aboraz Ruins, northeast of Booty Bay. He is exiled from his tribe. Why? Well...\nZanzil has methods of bending the minds of others, and his leaders fear him. He uses a mixture of jungle plants on his followers to suppress their will and strengthen their bodies.\nHis mixture would be worth much to those who wish to control others.\nBring me samples of his mixture, and I will find a use for them.","rew":"You will receive:\nBelt of Corruption\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Do you have the samples of Zanzil's Mixture??","done":"Ah, very good! Here is your pay.\nAnd here is a little something extra... for your discretion.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"4621":{"id":4621,"t":"Avast Ye, Admiral!","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Fleet Master Seahorn and Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay, and then return to Fleet Master Firallon aboard the Crimson Veil off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\nBaron Revilgaz slain\nFleet Master Seahorn slain\nReach 3000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","desc":"Listen close, sea dawg... the powers of Booty Bay is what keeps us Bloodsail from sailing wheres we like and taking whats we want as rights o' plunder. Were ye to put a knife to Fleet Master Seahorn, we'd ne'er run afoul of a Booty Bay's vessel. Were ye to put a knife to Baron Revilgaz, we'd ne'er face the law on their terms.\nIf ye are to be an honorary admiral amongst us - yes, ADMIRAL, you'll puts a knife to both of 'em as I've says. Go now lad/lass, and return to me once ye does the deeds.","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodsail Admiral's Hat\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers\n-1,000 reputation with Booty Bay","back":"Yer back already, ya blasted tar! Haves ye done as I've ordered? Fail us, and ye will be walkin' the plank.\nArrrrr...","done":"Avast ye... Admiral ‹name›! Yer a pirate of pirates, lass!\nIt warms the cackles of me heart to give ye this hat. Ye will ne'er find one like it anywheres, and all that gazes upon ye will see that yer an Admiral of the Bloodsail Navy!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":30.6,"y":90.6,"n":"Fleet Master Firallon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8061":{"id":8061,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Wraps","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Stanchion. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Stanchion\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"We Zandalar invest power in those who speak with the authority of divinity. Our priests are more than just healers - they are our confessors. Evil comes both from outside threats - such as Hakkar - and from within the tribe. Our confessors act as the judges amongst us, preserving us from the same evil that devoured the Gurubashi from inside itself.\nGo to Zul'Gurub and bring back the Paragons of Power from the Gurubashi. Learn what it means to be the confessor, and preserve us from evil.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Confessor's Wraps\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Back from Zul'Gurub, are you? Have you succeeded in retrieving the Paragons of Power from the minions of Hakkar?","done":"Outstanding, ‹name›! This was no small feat bringing these to me. No doubt you've acted as our tribe's confessor today in preserving ourselves against the threat of Hakkar. These wraps are befitting a friend of the tribe such as you!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1421":{"id":1421,"t":"The Lost Caravan","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Caravan Chest in the Fallow Sanctuary, obtain the Wizards' Reagents and bring to Watcher Biggs.\nWizards' Reagents Caravan Chest","desc":"I was stunned during the attack by the Lost Ones, but before my sight went black I spied one of our wagons being dragged to the Fallow Sanctuary, the lost one village to the north.\nA caravan chest with valuable reagents was in that wagon, reagents vital to the studies of the wizards of Nethergarde Keep. Find the chest and get those reagents, ‹name›. Get them and bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have the wizard's reagents, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, you found them! With these, the wizards in Nethergarde may continue their work. I do not know what it is that they do, but it is linked to the Dark Portal in the Blasted Lands, and is vital to the security of the Alliance.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26.7,"y":59.8,"n":"Watcher Biggs","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"2781":{"id":2781,"t":"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting","lv":46,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the head of Caliph Scorpidsting to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan.\nCaliph Scorpidsting's Head Caliph Scorpidsting","desc":"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting!\nThe Gadgetzan Water Company of Gadgetzan, Tanaris will pay a high bounty for the head of Caliph Scorpidsting, leader of the Wastewander outlaws. His crimes include:\n1. Murdering Gadgetzan Water Co. employees!\n2.Stealing Gadgetzan Water Co. resources!\n3.Seizing Gadgetzan Water Co. property!\nBring proof of Caliph Scorpidsting's demise to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle for an immediate reward!","rew":"Money: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Yes ‹class›, I am an official of the Gadgetzan Water Company. What can I assist you with?","done":"Finally - justice is served! You have struck a mighty blow against those vile nomads! With Scorpidsting's demise, this might be just the thing to finally push those squatters off of Gadgetzan's water wells!\nBy the authority of the Gadgetzan Water Company, I gladly award you with this bounty. You've done a great service for us all.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":27,"n":"Wanted Poster","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2541":{"id":2541,"t":"The Sleeping Druid","lv":8,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Shaman Voodoo Charm to Oben Rageclaw in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.\nShaman Voodoo Charm Gnarlpine Shaman 15 %","desc":"The Gnarlpine shaman that inhabit this place have discovered a way of separating a sleeping druid's spirit from the physical body. The furbolg have animated my physical form and are using it to attack anyone that attempts to explore the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. I am now trapped in the Emerald Dream, powerless to stop this.\nYou must help me. The Gnarlpine shaman carry a strange charm which is used to perform this ritual, and I'd like to examine it. Please, ‹name›, bring one to me.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"If I can examine the charm, I may be able to figure out how to break the enchantment. Have you found one?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›.\nWhat an odd trinket this is... I can sense the vile aura emanating from it; this is a very powerful enchantment.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":44.9,"y":61.6,"n":"Oben Rageclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"941":{"id":941,"t":"Planting the Heart","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Plant the Tainted Heart in Denalan's Planter.\nTainted Heart\nProvided: Tainted Heart","desc":"I have removed that foul moss from the heart, but it remains tainted...\nTry placing the heart in my planter. It is filled with a nutritive soil that may cleanse and heal the heart.","rew":"You will receive:\nCleansed Timberling Heart\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"This planter is filled with soil, specially prepared by Denalan.","done":"You place the heart within the planter, and it quickly digs itself in!\nA few seconds later it wriggles back out, cleansed. It pulses slightly... beckoning for you to take it.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.8,"y":68.6,"n":"Denalan's Planter","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"3661":{"id":3661,"t":"Favored of Elune?","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,200 experience instead of 6,000, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Collect 15 Wildkin Feathers from the Hinterlands for Erelas Ambersky in Rut'theran Village.\n15 Wildkin Feather Wildkin Feather","desc":"Wildkin are quite unpredictable creatures, ‹name›. Capable of incredible gentleness, these creatures will show extreme ferocity if something they deem important is threatened.\nThese beasts are rumored to have been created by Elune, and I am interested in finding if this is really the truth.\nRecently, I heard about a population of wildkin living in the Hinterlands -- Vicious, Primitive, and Savage Owlbeasts. They can be found amongst the wildlife there. Will you gather some wildkin feathers for me?","rew":"Money: 1 35 1 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Try to avoid them if you can, ‹name›. The Wildkin may misread your interest as an intent to do them harm...","done":"Thank you for bringing these to me, ‹name›.\nWhat did you learn of the Wildkin?\nPerhaps these feathers will tell us more. Ferocious monsters, or simply misguided pets? One day I'd like to know the truth...\nI am going to continue my research -- please come back and talk to me again after some time has passed.\nTeldrassil The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"3261":{"id":3261,"t":"Jorn Skyseer","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.","desc":"Your time with me is over, ‹name›. To learn more, you must go to Camp Taurajo to the south and speak with Jorn Skyseer. He will continue your guidance.","rew":"Experience: 140\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, young one. You are here to walk the hunter's path?\nVery good. Let us begin.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"6541":{"id":6541,"t":"Report to Kadrak","lv":19,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.","desc":"Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.\nIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders.","rew":"Experience: 150","done":"Ashenvale is a divided land, but our most recent efforts have been very successful. We not only have an outpost at the Zoram Strand, but another just north of here called Splintertree.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.1,"y":5.4,"n":"Kadrak","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1181":{"id":1181,"t":"Goblin Sponsorship","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.","desc":"I'm afraid I can't be of much more help to you, ‹name›. If you'd like to follow up on it more, I'd suggest you go hit up the Baron himself. If there's anyone who knows Revilgaz's business, it's Revilgaz.\nYou'll find him at the tavern across the harbor, top floor.","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"Oh, sure of course I know what you're talking about. Nope, can't help you though. Some of my men were supposed to go track down the blueprints for the fuel regulator, but they came back empty-handed.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.3,"y":73.6,"n":"Wharfmaster Lozgil","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7821":{"id":7821,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":42.7,"n":"Rumstag Proudstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3901":{"id":3901,"t":"Rattling the Rattlecages","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Rattlecage Skeletons, and then return to Shadow Priest Sarvis in Deathknell when you are done.\nRattlecage Skeleton slain : 0/ 12","desc":"You've shown your potential to the Forsaken under normal circumstances ‹name› - now let's see you under pressure.\nThe Rattlecage skeletons, more mindless minions of the Lich King, are a tougher foe than the zombies you have faced thus far. Again, thin their numbers and prove yourself to the Forsaken. Do not tarry - when you are done, speak to me again.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlax Boots Scavenger Tunic Roamer's Leggings\nExperience: 250\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Those who dally in this task might as well end up wandering about aimlessly like our fallen brothers and sisters in the village. Let's hope you will fare better than them, yes?","done":"I am finished with you, ‹name› - you have shown yourself to be worthy of the freedom that you have been given. Many will stand against you for what you have become, but know that no matter what they may try to do against us, we are free and will not be shackled again.\nTake these and be on your way. You have much to accomplish, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"381":{"id":381,"t":"The Scarlet Crusade","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Executor Arren 12 Scarlet Armbands from Scarlet Converts and Scarlet Initiates.\n12 Scarlet Armband Meven Korgal 80 % , Scarlet Initiate 80 % , Scarlet Convert 80 %","desc":"You'll be happy to know we appear to be making progress in the mine, thanks in no small part to your efforts. We can now turn our eyes to other concerns.\nMy scouts have reported that a detachment of the Scarlet Crusade is setting up a camp southeast of here. The Scarlet Crusade is a despicable organization that hunts us, and they will not rest until every undead--Lich King's Scourge or no--is destroyed. We must strike first!\nBe careful, their unholy zeal makes them dangerous adversaries.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nForsaken Dagger Forsaken Maul Forsaken Shortsword Forsaken Bastard Sword\nYou will also receive:\n5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Those fools... They happily send themselves to their own graves.","done":"If only they listened to reason, eh, ‹name›? Perhaps we could sit them down for reasonable discourse... ha!\nLight-blinded fools.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.2,"y":66,"n":"Executor Arren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"5901":{"id":5901,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.\nEmpty Termite Jar\n100 Plagueland Termites Large Termite Mound\nProvided: Empty Termite Jar","desc":"So, to bring pain and strife to the Scarlet Crusade, I want to take their precious lumber mill from them. I'm sure the loss of such a resource will cause them a great deal of harm in defending and rebuilding the town for their own reasons. Will you help me, ‹name›?\nStart by taking this jar to Plaguewood in the Eastern Plaguelands. Fill it with the termites you find in their mounds throughout the woods. Come back when you have enough.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Do you have the termites yet, ‹name›? I am sure it is obvious to a smart ‹class› like yourself.\nOnce we have enough of them, we'll make sure no one can use the lumber mill ever again!","done":"These will do nicely, ‹name›. Thank you.\nIf you're ready, we can get on with the next step.\nTirisfal Glades Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":72.3,"n":"Mickey Levine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4141":{"id":4141,"t":"Muigin and Larion","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 15 Bloodpetals and return to Muigin.\n15 Bloodpetal Bloodpetal Lasher 80 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 80 % , Bloodpetal Thresher 80 % , Bloodpetal Trapper 80 %","desc":"See Larion over there? It's HIS fault we're here!\nI told him we were going the wrong way, but would he listen? And would you believe that he's the one that won't speak to me? Well, until he changes his mind, let's have a bit of fun with him.\nHave you noticed the strange plant-like creatures around here? They're nothing but trouble, really, but I think if trained properly, I could get them to obey commands.\nFirst thing though, I'll need some samples to study. Do you think you could collect some?","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Larion's got something coming, that's for sure!","done":"I hope they didn't give you too much trouble, ‹name›. I try to steer clear of them -- they're wild!\nI tried jumping over one... I was attacked! Plants just shouldn't be acting that way!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":42.9,"y":9.6,"n":"Muigin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4381":{"id":4381,"t":"Crystal Restore","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Yellow Power Crystal Yellow Power Crystal , Yellow Power Crystal , Mor'vek 66.7 % , Gruff 0.6 % and 4 more\n10 Green Power Crystal Green Power Crystal , Green Power Crystal , Mor'vek 30.8 % , Spiked Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Restore","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine green power crystals with yellow power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to heal yourself or your allies.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":56.5,"y":12.5,"n":"Northern Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4301":{"id":4301,"t":"The Mighty U'cha","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring U'cha's Pelt to Torwa Pathfinder at the entrance of Un'Goro Crater.\nU'cha's Pelt U'cha","desc":"While you have been exploring Un'Goro, I have seen other things that a mighty hunter such as yourself would relish in. One such sight was a huge ape among the other gorillas to the north. You have been to that cave before, but this time, I wonder if you'll survive the encounter if you accept my task.\nI call him U'cha, and he is one of the Earth Mother's greatest sons, of that you can be sure. Defeat U'cha and bring me his pelt. Do this, and I will defend your right to call yourself a great hunter.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBeastsmasher Beastslayer\nExperience: 5,650","back":"U'cha... the beast was magnificent. Huge and red, with teeth the size of daggers. His arms as thick as tree trunks, and as fast as any mountain lion I have ever laid eyes upon. You should consider yourself lucky to find such a test of bravery--my people would go generations without seeing such a creature.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I am pleased. You have done a great thing here today.\nU'cha was one of the greatest apes I had ever seen. The fact that you have bested his strength speaks well of your own strength... and courage.\nIt is only fitting that I give you this as a sign of respect. You have earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1501":{"id":1501,"t":"Creature of the Void","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Tablet of Verga for Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nTablet of Verga Burning Blade Stash","desc":"So few warlocks remain... We risk much, but the risks are warranted. You must quickly reach maturity in your ability if you are to be of use to the Horde and to the Warchief.\nIt is time that you learned a new summoning spell.\nFirst, you must recover the Tablet of Verga, which was stolen by warlocks of the Burning Blade and is now kept at their lair in Skull Rock to the east of the city. With the tablet, I will show you the runes necessary to summoning a voidwalker.","rew":"Experience: 875","back":"Do you have the Tablet of Verga, ‹name›? If not, I do not wish to speak with you until you do.","done":"Good. I hope you inflicted some other losses on the Burning Blade when you went to retrieve this.\nThey have been a source of great annoyance for the Warchief, and a great blight upon warlocks as a whole.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4781":{"id":4781,"t":"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe","lv":34,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Gold Bar to Xizk Goodstitch in Stranglethorn Vale.\nGold Bar Tattered Chest 2 % , Battered Chest 0 % , Alliance Chest 0 % , Solid Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Your next task is as simple as your first, but will require you to seek out aid.\nI require gold thread for the embroidery of the cloak, but gold thread is not easy to come by, and very few know how to make it. Fortunately, one who is loyal to our cause knows its secrets and is willing to help those rising in our ranks.\nBring a gold bar to Xizk Goodstitch in Booty Bay. He is a master tailor and will be happy to spin the thread for you. Gold bars are smelted by skilled miners. Ask a miner for help.","rew":"Experience: 2,000","back":"Gold bars, yes... yes. Bring me one and we'll see what we can do about spinning some thread for you. Until then, I would suggest you focus your efforts on becoming more powerful. Your toughest trials are still ahead. And trust me... you'll wish you were more prepared, regardless of how powerful you think you might be.","done":"Perfect, ‹name›. I'm glad you could find a miner to help you out so quickly. Or did you do this work yourself? Either way, you've done well. This will be perfect for the thread.\nIt will take some time to create the stuff, so you'll have to come back--I actually send it off to some princess who we have locked in a tower who's only job is to spin gold thread... no, seriously. I mean it... okay, not really.\nThe Barrens Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.7,"y":76.9,"n":"Xizk Goodstitch","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7581":{"id":7581,"t":"The Prison's Bindings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Dire Maul in Feralas and recover 15 Satyr Blood from the Wildspawn Satyr that inhabit the Warpwood Quarter. Return to Daio in the Tainted Scar when this is done.\n15 Satyr Blood Wildspawn Hellcaller 80 % , Wildspawn Shadowstalker 80 % , Wildspawn Felsworn 80 % , Wildspawn Betrayer 80 % and 3 more","desc":"You must retrieve bindings for the prison of the Doomguard from lesser demons.\nThe blood of the Wildspawn satyr that occupy Dire Maul should do nicely. The coagulated blood will bond the Hederine shards and power the crystal prison.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Only the blood of Wildspawn satyr will suffice.","done":"Ah, a most excellent recovery. The blood will suppress the Doomguard's magical defenses.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":34.1,"y":50.1,"n":"Daio the Decrepit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1821":{"id":1821,"t":"Agamand Heirlooms","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Coleman Farthing the Agamand Family Axe, the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Mace and the Agamand Family dagger.\nAgamand Family Axe Agamand Weapon Rack\nAgamand Family Dagger Agamand Weapon Rack\nAgamand Family Mace Agamand Weapon Rack\nAgamand Family Sword Agamand Weapon Rack","desc":"The Agamand family were my employers in life, and they were the cause of my death! It is fitting that the Agamands are now mindless minions of the Lich King.\nNow I would have their last vestiges of honor. Go into their family crypt and rob them of their family heirlooms: a sword, an axe, a dagger and a mace. Bring them to me!\nThe Agamand family crypt is at the north end of the Agamand mills, protected by lurking scourge and dead Agamands.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Do you have the heirlooms, ‹name›?","done":"Ah! You retrieved them! Now the last semblance of honor and memory is stripped from the cursed Agamand lands. The family truly is no more!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5021":{"id":5021,"t":"Better Late Than Never","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The ramblings of the ghostly woman indicated that she needed a package delivered. She claimed that it was where her horse was. As to where the horse is or where the package was to be delivered - the ghost remains incomprehensible.","desc":"\"The package must be delivered... delivered before I'm trapped here!\"\nThe cries of a panicked woman feel almost like a whisper floating through the house. Cowered in the upstairs corner is the apparition of a woman. She does not seem to be fully cognizant of her surroundings, and she is only vaguely aware of you.\n\"Are you here to deliver my package? Please, before it gets much worse! I was going to ride out of here. It should still be by my horse... or am I too late?\"","rew":"Experience: 2,550","done":"A package in the barn that you might have otherwise overlooked now stands out amongst the decay and ruin. Perhaps this is the one that the ghost of Janice Felstone was clamoring about...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.4,"y":54.1,"n":"Janice Felstone","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.7,"y":55.2,"n":"Janice's Parcel","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"141":{"id":141,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Shaw's report to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\nShaw's Report\nProvided: Shaw's Report","desc":"The Stonemasons' Guild was run by a man named Edwin VanCleef. VanCleef was responsible for rebuilding Stormwind after the orcs razed it in the First War. Apparently, VanCleef and his men were unhappy with their treatment by the King after the reconstruction was complete. That just might explain a thing or two.\nI have written a more detailed account for your Master in Westfall. Take this to him at once!","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did Master Shaw shed any light on things?","done":"Edwin VanCleef. . .I know the name well. To think that a man so industrious and talented could turn into such a scoundrel unnerves me. I'll need further proof before I believe this.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98461":{"id":98461,"t":"Unrequited love","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Hollee's Note to Tarrel Rockweaver near Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.\nProvided: Hollee's Note","desc":"If you're heading out of Auberdine, I could use your help!\nMy dear friend Tarrel and I were classmates in school. Oh, he was such a quickfire on all things excavation! We got split up after graduation--him to Wetlands, and me to here in Darkshore.\n<Hollee sighs, then her brow furrows slightly.>\nSorry, and his wife... Merrin.\nIt doesn't matter. If you go to the Wetlands, could you make sure he's alright? And maybe give him this? He's probably near Menethil Harbor. There's a boat straight there.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 170","back":"What's all this about?","done":"<Tarrel reads the note.>\nOh... oh my. Poor Hollee.\nShe always did have a bit of a thing for me. And, truth be told, there was a time where I would have reciprocated. But I'm married. Happily married!\nI think the best thing to do here is not to reply. I don't know how to let her down, and I have far more pressing things to worry about here! My wife is missing!\nDarkshore Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":41.8,"n":"Archaeologist Hollee","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.4,"y":52.2,"n":"Tarrel Rockweaver","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98221":{"id":98221,"t":"From the ashes","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep wants you to destroy the 4 sets of Attack Plans in the Angerfang Encampment.\nAttack Plan: Menethil Harbor destroyed\nAttack Plan: Thelsamar destroyed\nAttack Plan: Southshore destroyed\nAttack Plan: Ironforge destroyed","desc":"In the Second War the Dragonmaw built a fleet where we now stand, intending to take Hillsbrad. They nearly succeeded!\nThey were routed by the red dragons, left to mere stragglers deep in the mountains. However, there has been a surge in activity in their encampment northeast of Menethil.\nDun Algaz is proof that they intend to march to war once again and retake this land. Find their attack plans, take note of any critical information, and destroy them. We need to know where they will strike next!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4861":{"id":4861,"t":"Enraged Wildkin","lv":59,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked camp and supplies in southern Winterspring.","desc":"Hey there, lad/lass! I was chased from my camp in southern Winterspring by some bloodthirsty wildkin! Well, I suppose I got too close to something the wildkin were guarding.\nI barely managed to get away safely; I fear a buddy of mine wasn't as lucky. Would you mind braving the wildkin and heading to the camp? I really need my supplies, and I'd also like to get back the amulet I unearthed yesterday at the dig site.","rew":"Experience: 3,200","done":"A severely damaged crate stands out among the rest of the destroyed belongings at the camp...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":52.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Jaron Stoneshaper","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":59,"y":59.8,"n":"Damaged Crate","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5981":{"id":5981,"t":"Rampaging Giants","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rivern Frostwind wants you to kill 4 Frostmaul Giants and 4 Frostmaul Preservers.\nFrostmaul Giant slain : 0/ 4\nFrostmaul Preserver slain : 0/ 4","desc":"Around 4,000 years ago, Tyrande Whisperwind saved the life of the frostsaber queen, at the hands of rampaging giants. Since then, the frostsabers have been allies of the night elves.\nThese same giants that once were a danger to the frostsabers, still exist not too far from here. They are called the frostmaul, and they have taken over the large valley to the south.\nProve your loyalty to the frostsabers; kill these giants in the name of the frostsaber queen, Shy-Rotam!","back":"You must continue to prove yourself, ‹name›.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. Your determination has been duly noted.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":49.9,"y":9.8,"n":"Rivern Frostwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92461":{"id":92461,"t":"Harmony in balance","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Vuldren Juveniles in Thendal Grove.\nJuvenile Vuldren slain : 0/ 8","desc":"We live in times of great uncertainty for our people. We face unprecedented challenges that may require bold solutions, but we also must contend with the ordinary and mundane here in Thendal Grove. Take, for example, the recent unsustainable rise in the vuldren population.\nThe vuldren are a vital part of our ecosystem. However, imbalances must be corrected to maintain the delicate harmony that all creatures in Thendal Grove share.\nHead east and cull some of the vuldren there.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFur-Lined Shoes Vuldren Hide Bracers\nMoney: 15 0 gold, 0 silver, 15 copper Experience: 80\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"Thank you for your service to Zephras, young ‹class›.\nThe vuldren are typically quite docile, but the animals that call Zephras home can sense when the magic on the winds is out of balance, which can lead to dangerous and unpredictable behavior if left unchecked.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92701":{"id":92701,"t":"To valanaar","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.\nProvided: Aonda's Written Report","desc":"For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to the Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, ‹name›.","back":"A letter from Aonda. What's that crafty highlander been up to?","done":"<Valennia's expression darkens as she reads the letter.>\nAonda trusted you to deliver this and she speaks highly enough of you in this letter, so I'll try to trust you too. Before we speak further, I need to consult with the few peacekeepers I have left here and formulate a plan in case the cult strikes here next. Enjoy your stay in Valanaar for now.\nIf you are looking to keep yourself busy, there are plenty of townsfolk that can likely use the help of a strong young adventurer like yourself.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2861":{"id":2861,"t":"Tabetha's Task","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"Rumor is that Tabetha, a mage colleague who lives deep in Dustwallow Marsh, has a bone to pick with a certain sand troll in Zul'Farrak. If you speak with Tabetha she can tell you more.\nAnd bring some friends with you, ‹name›. If Tabetha has you go to Zul'Farrak then you're not going to want to go alone.\nYou will find Tabetha's cottage west of Theramore, and just north of the Stonemaul Ruin.","rew":"Experience: 410","done":"That's right. I do have a bone to pick with a troll. A few bones. All her bones!\nWant to help me?\nThunder Bluff Undercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Orgrimmar Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.7,"y":14.2,"n":"Ursyn Ghull","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":22.4,"n":"Bink","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.4,"y":86.1,"n":"Deino","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8141":{"id":8141,"t":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalarian Shadow Talisman\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"You progress swiftly, young ‹class›. Perhaps it is time to initiate you into the Shera Ali'kh - Zandalari for Death's Hand. For thousands of years we have played the role of assassin for the Zandalar Empire. For too long we have sat idly, allowing the Hakkari to grow in strength. Once more we face Hakkar, but this time without the support of a united ‹race› front. It is you and your allies who must assist in vanquishing the Blood God and his minions!\nWear this talisman and let it assist you in your journeys.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});